mixin () {
  /// Returns static Markdown documentation for this backend's public API.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Birthday Wish Backend API\n\nThis canister stores and serves all editable content for the romantic birthday wish site: the hero greeting, the ordered sequence of animated messages (each optionally paired with a photo), and the single background song. Photos and the song are stored via platform object storage; this canister stores only their `StoredFile` references. Each photo may carry saved crop/adjust parameters that the frontend applies when rendering.\n\n## Types\n\n- `StoredFile = Storage.ExternalBlob` (a `Blob`) — an off-chain file reference managed by platform object storage. The frontend uploads the bytes and passes the resulting blob to the mutation methods; the canister stores only the reference. The frontend resolves it to a display URL via the object-storage client.\n- `CropAdjust = { zoom : Float; offsetX : Float; offsetY : Float; rotation : Float }` — saved crop/adjust parameters for a photo. `zoom` is a scale factor (1.0 = fit), `offsetX`/`offsetY` are fractions of the rendered width/height, and `rotation` is in degrees. All values are normalized so they are independent of the rendered size.\n- `Message = { id : Nat; text : Text; photo : ?StoredFile; crop : ?CropAdjust; position : Nat }` — one animated message. `position` controls display order (ascending). `crop` is `null` until the owner saves adjustments for that message's photo.\n- `Greeting = { headline : Text; subtext : Text; heroPhoto : ?StoredFile; heroCrop : ?CropAdjust }` — the hero section content.\n- `SongSource = { kind : { #url; #upload; #default }; url : ?Text; file : ?StoredFile }` — the active background song source. `#url` means an owner-set external URL (takes precedence), `#upload` means an owner-uploaded file, and `#default` means neither is set and the frontend plays its bundled default theme song.\n- `SiteContent = { greeting : Greeting; messages : [Message]; song : ?StoredFile; songSource : SongSource }` — the full public payload. `messages` is returned sorted by `position` ascending.\n- `MessageInput = { text : Text; photo : ?StoredFile; crop : ?CropAdjust; position : Nat }`\n- `GreetingInput = { headline : Text; subtext : Text }`\n\n## Public reads\n\n### `getSiteContent() : async SiteContent` (query)\n\nReturns the complete site content. This is a **query** call: it is fast, unreplicated, and read-only. It requires no authentication — anonymous callers receive the same content as signed-in callers. `messages` is sorted by `position` ascending; ties keep their map iteration order. `song`, `songSource`, and any `photo`/`crop` are `null` until the owner sets them.\n\n### `getSongSource() : async SongSource` (query)\n\nReturns the active background song source. Requires no authentication. When `kind` is `#default`, the frontend plays its bundled default theme song; when `#upload`, it plays the stored `file`; when `#url`, it plays the external `url`. This is what lets autoplay apply uniformly to both the owner's uploaded song and the default theme song.\n\n## Owner-only mutations\n\nAll mutation methods require the caller to be an **admin** of the canister's authorization state. The first caller to initialize access control becomes the owner/admin; subsequent callers are not. An unauthorized caller receives a trap with the message `Unauthorized: owner only`. These are update calls and persist their changes.\n\n### `updateGreeting(input : GreetingInput) : async Greeting`\n\nUpdates the hero headline and subtext. The hero photo and its saved crop are preserved.\n\n### `setHeroPhoto(photo : StoredFile) : async Greeting`\n\nSets or replaces the hero photo. Any crop saved for the previous photo is cleared, so stale adjustments never apply to a new image.\n\n### `setHeroCrop(crop : CropAdjust) : async Bool`\n\nSaves crop/adjust parameters for the hero photo. Returns `false` when no hero photo is set (nothing to crop); returns `true` on success. Re-opening the photo in the owner panel restores these saved values.\n\n### `addMessage(input : MessageInput) : async Nat`\n\nAdds a message and returns its assigned id. `crop` may be `null`.\n\n### `updateMessage(id : Nat, input : MessageInput) : async Bool`\n\nReplaces a message's text, photo, crop, and position. Returns `false` when the id is unknown.\n\n### `setMessageCrop(id : Nat, crop : CropAdjust) : async Bool`\n\nSaves crop/adjust parameters for a message's photo. Returns `false` when the message is unknown or has no photo; `true` on success.\n\n### `deleteMessage(id : Nat) : async Bool`\n\nDeletes a message. Returns `false` when the id is unknown.\n\n### `setSong(file : StoredFile) : async StoredFile`\n\nSets or replaces the uploaded background song file.\n\n### `setSongUrl(url : Text) : async SongSource`\n\nSets an external audio URL, which takes precedence over any uploaded file. Traps with `Invalid audio URL: must start with http:// or https://` when the URL is not a plausible http(s) URL.\n\n### `clearSongUrl() : async SongSource`\n\nClears the external audio URL, reverting to the uploaded song (or the default theme song when none is uploaded).\n\n## Authentication and identity\n\nReads (`getSiteContent`, `getSongSource`, `getApiDoc`) are open to anonymous callers. Every mutation requires a signed (non-anonymous) caller that is an admin of the canister's authorization state. The app's frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available; an agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n\nRegistration gates access: a direct API caller must call `_initialize_access_control` once as a signed-in caller before any role-guarded call, including guarded queries. The first initializer receives the admin/owner role; subsequent callers do not. An unregistered or anonymous caller receives a trap with the message `Unauthorized: owner only` on guarded endpoints. A caller can be unregistered while assuming the app already knows it because registration happens only when a caller signs in through the app's own frontend, so a principal that never did so is unregistered even when it belongs to the app's owner, and a signed-in caller derived against a different origin is a different principal than the one the frontend registered.\n\n## Errors and limits\n\n- Unauthorized mutations trap with `Unauthorized: owner only`.\n- `setSongUrl` traps with `Invalid audio URL: must start with http:// or https://` for a malformed URL.\n- `setHeroCrop` and `setMessageCrop` return `false` rather than trapping when there is no photo to crop.\n- Mutations are not idempotent in general: `addMessage` always creates a new entry, so retrying a failed call can duplicate a message. `updateMessage`, `setHeroPhoto`, `setSong`, and the crop setters are safe to retry with the same arguments.\n";
  };
};
